Git vs GitHub

| Feature                 | **Git**                              | **GitHub**                           |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------ |
| **What is it?**         | Version control system               | Online platform for Git repositories |
| **Main purpose**        | Tracks changes in code               | Stores and shares code online        |
| **Where does it work?** | Your local computer                  | Cloud / Internet                     |
| **Internet required?**  | ❌ No                                 | ✅ Yes                                |
| **Installation**        | Must be installed on your computer   | No installation; use website         |
| **Tracks code history** | ✅ Yes                                | Displays and stores Git history      |
| **Main commands**       | `git add`, `git commit`, `git merge` | Repository, Pull Request, Actions    |
| **Collaboration**       | Possible, but mainly local tracking  | Easy team collaboration              |
| **CI/CD**               | Does not provide CI/CD itself        | GitHub Actions can automate CI/CD    |
| **Example**             | `git commit -m "Added chatbot"`      | Push project to a GitHub repository  |



===========

